# MULTIPLAYER FRONTEND IMPLEMENTATION

## Architecture Overview

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Phase 1: Data Layer"
        Store["useRaceStore"] --> Service["multiplayerApi"]
    end
    subgraph "Phase 2: Observer"
        LobbyHook["useLobbyPolling"] --> Store
    end
    subgraph "Phase 3: Reactive UI"
        ReadyOverlay["ReadyUpOverlay"] --> Service
        ReadyOverlay --> Store
    end
    subgraph "Phase 4: Engine"
        SyncHook["useRaceSync"] --> Store
    end
    subgraph "Phase 5: After-Action"
        Results["ResultsModal"] --> Store
    end

    LobbyHook -.->|"COUNTDOWN: Kill"| SyncHook
    SyncHook -.->|"FINISHED: Trigger"| Results
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **The Golden Rule:** Only one polling hook may own the Zustand store at any time. The [RacePage](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/app/race/%5BroomId%5D/page.tsx#23-224) acts as the switch.

---

## Phase 1: Persistence & Data Layer

> The foundation. Nothing can render, poll, or persist without the data contracts being defined first.

### Step 1.1 — Expand [useRaceStore.ts](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/store/useRaceStore.ts)

**Rationale:** Every UI component and hook reads from this single Zustand store. Adding the new fields first means every downstream consumer can be built against a stable contract, even before the hooks that populate them exist.

#### Input/Output Contract

```typescript
// New fields to add to RaceState
interface RaceStateAdditions {
  role: 'host' | 'guest' | null;       // Set on room rehydration
  hostReady: boolean;                   // From lobby poll
  guestReady: boolean;                  // From lobby poll
  opponentName: string | null;          // From room data
  persistenceStatus: PersistenceStatus; // Set by save trigger
}

type PersistenceStatus = 'IDLE' | 'SAVING' | 'SAVED' | 'ALREADY_SAVED' | 'ERROR';
```

#### Internal State Logic

| Action | Trigger | Effect |
|--------|---------|--------|
| [setGameState(partial)](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/store/useRaceStore.ts#56-57) | Any hook response | Merges partial state into store |
| [updateLocalProgress(p, wpm)](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/store/useRaceStore.ts#58-67) | `TypeInput.onInput` | Sets `localProgress`, `localWpm`, flips `localFinished` at 100 |
| [resetStore()](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/store/useRaceStore.ts#68-69) | Page unmount | Resets all fields to `initialState` including new additions |

#### Changes Required

Add these to `initialState`:
```typescript
role: null,
hostReady: false,
guestReady: false,
opponentName: null,
persistenceStatus: 'IDLE',
```

Add [GameState](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/store/useRaceStore.ts#3-4) enum value: `'WAITING_FOR_GUEST' | 'LOBBY_FULL' | 'READY_CHECK'` alongside existing states.

---

### Step 1.2 — Create `multiplayerApi.ts`

**Rationale:** Separating API calls from hooks follows the same pattern as [raceApi.ts](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/services/raceApi.ts) (solo). Hooks orchestrate *when* to call; the service handles *how*. This makes unit testing hooks trivial — you mock `multiplayerApi` instead of [fetch](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/app/race/%5BroomId%5D/page.tsx#51-72).

#### Method Contracts

```typescript
// src/services/multiplayerApi.ts

export interface CreateRoomResponse {
  roomId: string;
  hostId: string;
  room: RaceData;           // Full Redis-parsed room state
}

export interface JoinRoomResponse {
  roomId: string;
  guestId: string;
  room: RaceData;
}

export interface ReadyUpResponse {
  roomId: string;
  room: RaceData;           // Contains updated host_ready / guest_ready
}

export interface StartRaceResponse {
  roomId: string;
  targetStartMs: number;
  serverNowMs: number;
  status: 'STARTING' | 'ALREADY_STARTING';
}

export interface LobbyHeartbeatResponse {
  roomId: string;
  serverNowMs: number;      // ← Critical for clock offset
  room: {
    host_id: string;
    guest_id: string | null;
    status: string;
    is_guest_ready: boolean;
    target_start_ms: number;
    prompt_text: string;
    is_opponent_disconnected: boolean;
  };
}

export interface SaveResultsResponse {
  status: 'SAVED' | 'ALREADY_SAVED';
}
```

**Error Contract:** Every method throws a typed error with `status` code:
```typescript
export class MultiplayerApiError extends Error {
  constructor(public status: number, message: string) {
    super(message);
  }
}
```

