## Phase 2: The "Observer" Layer

> This layer is the "eyes" of the frontend during the lobby phase. It watches Redis via the heartbeat endpoint and synchronizes the client's clock before the race begins.

### Step 2.1 — Create `useLobbyPolling.ts`

**Rationale:** The lobby phase (WAITING → LOBBY_FULL → READY_CHECK → COUNTDOWN) is low-frequency (2-3s polls) and reads *different data* than the high-frequency race sync. Separating them:
1. Prevents the race sync Lua script from being hit while in WAITING state (wasted Redis ops)
2. Allows the lobby to calculate `clockOffsetMs` early, so the countdown is accurate from frame 1
3. Enforces the "Single Source of Truth" constraint — only one writer at a time

#### Input/Output Contract

```typescript
// Input Props
interface LobbyPollingParams {
  roomId: string | null;
  userId: string | null;
  enabled: boolean;           // The "switch" — false when race phase starts
}

// Output (returned to RacePage)
interface LobbyPollingResult {
  isPolling: boolean;
  error: Error | null;
}
```

#### Internal State Logic

```typescript
// useEffect dependencies: [roomId, userId, enabled]
// Polling Interval: 2500ms

useEffect(() => {
  if (!enabled || !roomId) return;
  
  const intervalId = setInterval(async () => {
    const data = await multiplayerApi.lobbyHeartbeat(roomId, userId);
    
    // 1. Clock Offset (CRITICAL — must happen BEFORE countdown)
    const clockOffsetMs = data.serverNowMs - Date.now();
    
    // 2. Write to store (this is the ONLY writer during lobby)
    setGameState({
      state: data.room.status as GameState,
      hostReady: /* derive from room data */,
      guestReady: data.room.is_guest_ready,
      targetStartMs: data.room.target_start_ms || null,
      clockOffsetMs,
    });
  }, 2500);

  // CLEANUP: Hard kill on unmount or when `enabled` flips to false
  return () => clearInterval(intervalId);
}, [roomId, userId, enabled]);
```

> [!CAUTION]
> **The Clock Offset calculation MUST happen in the lobby hook, not in [useRaceSync](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/hooks/useRaceSync.ts#23-103).** The countdown UI reads `targetStartMs` adjusted by `clockOffsetMs`. If the offset isn't calculated until the first sync pulse (500ms into the countdown), the user will see a jarring jump in the countdown timer.

#### Cleanup Contract

| Trigger | Action |
|---------|--------|
| `enabled` becomes `false` | `clearInterval` immediately |
| Component unmount | `clearInterval` via useEffect return |
| `state === 'COUNTDOWN'` detected in poll response | Parent sets `enabled = false` (the Hook Handover) |

---

### Step 2.2 — Wire the Hook Handover in [RacePage](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/app/race/%5BroomId%5D/page.tsx#23-224)

**Rationale:** The [RacePage](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/app/race/%5BroomId%5D/page.tsx#23-224) is the "Scheduler" — it decides which hook is active based on the current [GameState](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/store/useRaceStore.ts#3-4). This is where the "Single Source of Truth" constraint is enforced.

```typescript
// RacePage.tsx — The Switch
const gameState = useRaceStore((s) => s.state);

const isLobbyPhase = 
  gameState === 'WAITING_FOR_GUEST' || 
  gameState === 'LOBBY_FULL' || 
  gameState === 'READY_CHECK';

// Phase 2 hook: active during lobby only
useLobbyPolling({
  roomId,
  userId,
  enabled: isLobbyPhase,
});

// Phase 4 hook: active during race only
useRaceSync({
  roomId,
  userId,
  currentProgress: localProgress,
  currentWpm: localWpm,
  enabled: !isLobbyPhase && gameState !== 'FINISHED',
});
```

---

### Phase 2 Definition of Done

- [ ] `useLobbyPolling` polls `GET /api/race/lobby/[id]` every 2.5s when `enabled = true`
- [ ] `clockOffsetMs` is written to the store on every poll response
- [ ] Polling stops immediately when `enabled` flips to `false`
- [ ] No two intervals are ever active simultaneously
- [ ] **Verification:** Open two browser tabs to the same room URL. Tab 1 (Host) creates, Tab 2 (Guest) navigates to the link. Observe in DevTools Network tab:
  - Lobby heartbeat requests fire at ~2.5s intervals
  - Once state becomes `COUNTDOWN`, lobby requests stop and sync requests begin at 500ms

