## Phase 3: The "Reactive" UI

> This layer translates store state into interactive UI elements. It handles the Ready/Start handshake that bridges the lobby and the race.

### Step 3.1 — Create `ReadyUpOverlay.tsx`

**Rationale:** The current [RacePage](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/app/race/%5BroomId%5D/page.tsx#23-224) has a static "Awaiting Opponent" overlay. The ready-up flow requires three distinct visual states within the lobby phase, each with different interactive elements.

#### Input/Output Contract

```typescript
interface ReadyUpOverlayProps {
  roomId: string;
  userId: string | null;
  onStartTriggered: () => void;   // Callback when countdown begins
}
```

#### Internal State Machine

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> WAITING_FOR_GUEST
    WAITING_FOR_GUEST --> LOBBY_FULL: Guest joins (via lobby poll)
    LOBBY_FULL --> READY_CHECK: Both players ready (via ready API)
    READY_CHECK --> COUNTDOWN: Start API called (auto-trigger)
    COUNTDOWN --> [*]: Overlay dismissed
```

#### UI States

| Store State | UI Rendered | Interactive Elements |
|------------|-------------|---------------------|
| `WAITING_FOR_GUEST` | Spinner + "Awaiting Opponent" | Copy Invite Link button |
| `LOBBY_FULL` | Two player cards with ready badges | **"Ready Up"** button (calls `POST /api/race/ready`) |
| `READY_CHECK` | "Both Ready! Launching..." | None (auto-triggers `POST /api/race/multiplayer-start`) |

#### Key useEffect: Auto-Start Trigger

```typescript
// When both players are ready, auto-call the start endpoint
useEffect(() => {
  if (gameState !== 'READY_CHECK') return;

  const triggerStart = async () => {
    const result = await multiplayerApi.startRace(roomId, userId);
    // Write countdown data to store
    setGameState({
      state: 'COUNTDOWN',
      targetStartMs: result.targetStartMs,
      clockOffsetMs: result.serverNowMs - Date.now(),
    });
    onStartTriggered();
  };

  triggerStart();
}, [gameState]); // Only fires when state transitions TO READY_CHECK
```

> [!NOTE]
> **Why either player can trigger start:** The `MULTIPLAYER_START` Lua script is idempotent. If both players' frontends call it simultaneously, the first gets `OK` and the second gets `ALREADY_STARTING` with the same `targetStartMs`. Both are success states.

---

### Step 3.2 — Wire Auto-Join Logic in [RacePage](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/app/race/%5BroomId%5D/page.tsx#23-224)

**Rationale:** When a Guest navigates to `/race/[roomId]`, they need to automatically join the room. Currently [RacePage](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/app/race/%5BroomId%5D/page.tsx#23-224) only rehydrates — it doesn't call the join endpoint.

```typescript
// RacePage.tsx — On mount, determine role and auto-join if guest
useEffect(() => {
  const initRoom = async () => {
    const roomData = await multiplayerApi.getRoom(roomId);
    
    if (roomData.room.host_id === userId) {
      // I'm the host
      setGameState({ role: 'host', state: roomData.room.state });
    } else {
      // I'm a guest — attempt to join
      const joinResult = await multiplayerApi.joinRoom(roomId, userId);
      setGameState({ role: 'guest', state: joinResult.room.state });
    }
  };
  initRoom();
}, [roomId]);
```

---

### Phase 3 Definition of Done

- [ ] `ReadyUpOverlay` renders three visual states matching the table above
- [ ] Clicking "Ready Up" calls `POST /api/race/ready` and updates the store
- [ ] When both players are ready, `POST /api/race/multiplayer-start` is auto-called
- [ ] The `ALREADY_STARTING` response is handled gracefully (no error toast)
- [ ] Guest auto-joins on page load; Host skips the join call
- [ ] **Verification:** Two-tab test:
  1. Tab 1: Create room → see "Awaiting Opponent" overlay
  2. Tab 2: Navigate to room URL → auto-joins → both tabs see "LOBBY_FULL" overlay
  3. Both tabs click "Ready Up" → overlay transitions to "Launching..."
  4. Countdown begins on both tabs simultaneously (within 1s tolerance)

